      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-28T12:25:00Z",
      "note": "Reviewed all three campaign transactions and traces, commit-pinned reproduction, reconstructed vulnerable source, proxy deployment and complete Upgraded history, historical implementation slots and runtimes, and stablecoin transfers. Transaction 0x0adf9953c4e2506ffd4526ceee962a9bb61c573eaef60f669605cca68d0ef5aa creates the borrower helper and calls requestCredit on all three pools. Anchor 0x7126ae1d8e8d1e0c0f1c598de16a035cf309d6cc556e73edc2847de2b5777e5e calls refreshAccount(borrower) on each pool, producing the first Requested-to-GoodStanding transitions without Evaluation Agent approval. Transaction 0x7b8d641d76affcc029fd0e0f06ab81ad675b1da21ef79b82e1343016040ba359 later calls drawdown on each pool and transfers exactly 82315.571143 USDC and 19074.730401 USDC.e to the attacker. The representative pool delegates to a 16,546-byte implementation whose runtime hash is 0x0bdbab48066bd5f42bb6aef5d687bd933a2a2bb804ee929cb4dac67ed6967ba9 at activation block 44526523 and pre-anchor block 86725371. Its creation-block Upgraded event is its only one before the anchor, and the EIP-1967 slot remains 0x57107d02c2b70e09ad77240dbde7ad77fe91ea1c. The two sibling pools execute the same failure and are covered by the representative-target rule. Code age is 90,358,155 seconds."
    }
